From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:46:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: no frame counted in flight for a wcid that's
 being published

wcid->non_aql_packets counts a station's frames in the hardware that
mac80211's airtime accounting doesn't cover (management frames, null
frames). It goes up when such a frame is queued and down when its
completion finds the wcid by its index.

A full reset can leave it one too high. mt7915_mac_restart() clears
MT76_RESET and lets the tx worker run again before mt76_reset_device()
unpublishes the stations, so a management frame that waited in a
station's tx_pending through the firmware's hang can be sent in between
and counted, and its completion then finds no wcid. The station, and
its counter, outlive the reset, and nothing ever set the counter back.

With frames held for dozing stations (MT_DRV_HW_PS_BUFFERING),
mt76_tx_ps_busy() takes a count above zero as a frame in flight: such a
station would get no frame at all while it dozes, so no TIM bit either,
until it happens to wake by itself, for as long as it stays associated.
At 16 its txqs are never served.

mt76_wcid_init() sets the count to zero: nothing is in flight for a wcid
about to be published, the first time or after a reset.

mt76_test_sta_readd_after_reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mac80211.c        | 10 ++++++++++
 tests/core-test.c |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index 4f75e018..c5ea4894 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1846,6 +1846,16 @@ void mt76_wcid_init(struct mt76_wcid *wcid, u8 band_idx)
 {
 	wcid->hw_key_idx = -1;
 	wcid->phy_idx = band_idx;
+	/*
+	 * Nothing is in flight for a wcid about to be published. For a station
+	 * mac80211 re-adds after a full reset this isn't 0 by itself: the tx
+	 * worker runs again before the reset unpublishes the stations, and a
+	 * management frame it sent one from tx_pending in between was counted,
+	 * while its completion found no wcid to count it off. One left over
+	 * would keep the station from ever getting a frame while it dozes
+	 * (mt76_tx_ps_busy()), for as long as it stays associated.
+	 */
+	atomic_set(&wcid->non_aql_packets, 0);
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&wcid->tx_list);
 	skb_queue_head_init(&wcid->tx_pending);
diff --git a/tests/core-test.c b/tests/core-test.c
index b000eb80..ce06cfc4 100644
--- a/tests/core-test.c
+++ b/tests/core-test.c
@@ -3481,6 +3481,10 @@ static void mt76_test_sta_readd_after_reset(struct kunit *test)
 	mt76_reset_device(dev);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_NULL(test, rcu_access_pointer(dev->wcid[9]));
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt76_test_sched.n, 0);
+	/* A management frame the tx worker sent it between the restart and the
+	 * reset of the stations: counted, and its completion found no wcid.
+	 */
+	atomic_set(&wcid->non_aql_packets, 1);
 
 	/* mac80211's restart work re-adds it */
 	runs = atomic_read(&mt76_test_worker_runs);
@@ -3488,6 +3492,8 @@ static void mt76_test_sta_readd_after_reset(struct kunit *test)
 					     IEEE80211_STA_NOTEXIST,
 					     IEEE80211_STA_NONE), 0);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_PTR_EQ(test, rcu_access_pointer(dev->wcid[9]), wcid);
+	/* nothing of its is in flight: not held back for that frame for good */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atomic_read(&wcid->non_aql_packets), 0);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt76_test_sched.n, 2);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_PTR_EQ(test, mt76_test_sched.txq[0], sta->txq[0]);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_PTR_EQ(test, mt76_test_sched.txq[1], sta->txq[1]);
